    {
     "claim": "B_escapes",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "Bundy escaped custody twice in Colorado in 1977: on 7 June 1977 he jumped from a second-floor law-library window of the Pitkin County Courthouse in Aspen during a hearing; on 30 December 1977 he escaped from the Garfield County Jail in Glenwood Springs through an opening in his cell ceiling (where a light fixture had been) into a crawl space.",
     "urls": [
      "https://umbrasearch.org/catalog/387fb662e67ee346f9b254c87a3e31e8bd2c812f",
      "https://www.biography.com/crime/a81984931/ted-bundy-timeline-murders",
      "https://www.crimeandinvestigation.co.uk/article/ted-bundy-rapist-serial-killer-escape-artist",
      "https://www.denvergazette.com/2022/05/04/looking-back-infamous-serial-killer-escapes-custody-twice-in-colorado-mountains/",
      "https://www.durangoherald.com/?p=41076",
      "https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/november-8/ted-bundy-botches-an-abduction-attempt"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "B_stops",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "Both escapes ended at a traffic stop in a stolen car: about six days after the Aspen escape, officers pulled over the stolen car he was driving (June 1977); after the jail escape, a Pensacola police officer stopped the stolen Volkswagen he was driving (15 February 1978). With the August 1975 Utah stop, traffic stops figured in three of his arrests.",
     "urls": [
      "https://www.crimeandinvestigation.co.uk/article/ted-bundy-rapist-serial-killer-escape-artist",
      "https://www.denvergazette.com/2022/05/04/looking-back-infamous-serial-killer-escapes-custody-twice-in-colorado-mountains/",
      "https://9news.com/article/news/ted-bundy-a-look-at-the-colorado-connection-to-the-notorious-serial-killer/73-c2c3b551-9a55-4d24-af5e-4471d1d1d65b",
      "https://aspentimes.com/news/author-releases-new-book-about-ted-bundys-six-days-in-aspen",
      "https://umbrasearch.org/catalog/387fb662e67ee346f9b254c87a3e31e8bd2c812f",
      "https://www.oxygen.com/martinis-murder/where-did-ted-bundy-get-caught-how-was-he-captured",
      "https://kutv.com/news/nation-world/bundys-last-stop-recounting-a-serial-killers-arrest-40-years-later-02-14-2018"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "B_hero",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "The car of the 1975 stop was Bundy's tan 1968 Volkswagen Beetle (now displayed at the Alcatraz East Crime Museum); the 1978 car was a stolen orange Beetle. Our hero object is a generic Beetle-shaped car with no badge and a blank plate.",
     "urls": [
      "https://alcatrazeast.com/inside-alcatraz-east/artifacts/ted-bundy-volkswagen/",
      "https://news.yahoo.com/ted-bundy-apos-world-apos-100000543.html",
      "https://archive.seattletimes.com/archive/19970716/2549799/ex-deputy-tries-to-cash-in-bundys-car----victims-parents-upset-by-attempt-to-sell-serial-killers-volkswagen",
      "https://mail.crimelibrary.org/serial_killers/notorious/bundy/13.html"
     ]
    }
   ],
